            <ArticleTitle>Factors Associated With Removal of Urinary Catheters After Surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NCQ.0000000000000287</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Publicly available data from the Centers for Medicaid &amp; Medicare Services were used to analyze factors associated with removal of the urinary catheter within 48 hours after surgery in 59 Massachusetts hospitals. Three factors explained 36% of the variance in postoperative urinary catheter removal: fewer falls per 1000 discharges, better nurse-patient communication, and higher percentage of Medicare patients. Timely urinary catheter removal was significantly greater in hospitals with more licensed nursing hours per patient day.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
